00:21:13,421 --> 00:21:14,254
"Did I tell ya I can read lips?

518
00:21:14,254 --> 00:21:16,671
"I'm reading lips right now."

519
00:21:20,175 --> 00:21:22,675
- [Tom] "Naughty little girl."

520
00:21:29,008 --> 00:21:30,925
- [Crow] Sam Donaldson.

521
00:21:34,762 --> 00:21:37,595
- [Joel] Tales from the dark side.

522
00:21:39,628 --> 00:21:43,402
- [Tom] "They need
coffee in there, quick!"

523
00:21:43,402 --> 00:21:44,437
- [Crow] "It's Michael Cane,

524
00:21:44,437 --> 00:21:45,828
"look out!"

525
00:21:45,828 --> 00:21:47,188
- [Joel] "Well that was easy.

526
00:21:47,188 --> 00:21:51,105
"Jeeze, I'm already
running ahead of schedule."

527
00:21:54,624 --> 00:21:56,215
- [Tom] "I wonder who that could-- ow!"

528
00:21:56,215 --> 00:21:57,048
- Get out.

529
00:21:57,048 --> 00:21:57,881
Just hurry.

530
00:21:57,881 --> 00:21:59,789
- Right.

531
00:21:59,789 --> 00:22:00,896
- [Crow] "We just came
to beat everybody up.

532
00:22:00,896 --> 00:22:03,229
"We're leaving now, thanks."

533
00:22:06,576 --> 00:22:08,962
- I hate to be interrupted
when I give a lecture.

534
00:22:08,962 --> 00:22:11,872
- [Tom] Poor Jud Fry is dead.

535
00:22:11,872 --> 00:22:13,762
(chatter)

536
00:22:13,762 --> 00:22:16,512
(romantic music)

537
00:22:17,882 --> 00:22:19,042
- This man is dead.

538
00:22:19,042 --> 00:22:19,875
- [Joel] No duh.

539
00:22:19,875 --> 00:22:22,682
- Yes, unfortunately I
found myself distracted.

540
00:22:22,682 --> 00:22:25,376
So I used the sublime attemi.

541
00:22:25,376 --> 00:22:26,216
It's fatal.

542
00:22:26,216 --> 00:22:27,299
- Don't tell me, doctor,

543
00:22:27,299 --> 00:22:30,486
that there's anything that
would be able to distract you.

544
00:22:30,486 --> 00:22:31,566
- Oh yes, for instance,

545
00:22:31,566 --> 00:22:34,060
when a charming girl keeps
gazing out of the window

546
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:35,620
while a brawl's going on.

547
00:22:35,620 --> 00:22:36,646
- [Tom] (chuckles) Get it?

548
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:38,553
- It's your fault if my jaw is broken.

549
00:22:38,553 --> 00:22:39,886
- Oh, I'm sorry.

550
00:22:39,886 --> 00:22:41,633
But what can I do to make it up to you?

551
00:22:41,633 --> 00:22:42,500
- [Crow] "Paint my house?"

552
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:43,513
- What do you suggest?

553
00:22:43,513 --> 00:22:44,500
- [Joel] Come on, you guys, let's go.

554
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:46,393
- [Tom] I've got an idea
for a kind of neat scenario

555
00:22:46,393 --> 00:22:47,913
or a scene, maybe.

556
00:22:47,913 --> 00:22:50,580
(doors closing)

557
00:22:57,953 --> 00:23:00,393
- Joel's really gone off
the deep end this time.

558
00:23:00,393 --> 00:23:01,226
- I'll say.

559
00:23:01,226 --> 00:23:02,393
- All I know is in this outfit

560
00:23:02,393 --> 00:23:04,140
I feel like a total femme.

561
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:04,973
You know what?

562
00:23:04,973 --> 00:23:08,730
I don't have a problem with it. (laughs)

563
00:23:08,730 --> 00:23:12,230
('60s action movie music)

564
00:23:30,546 --> 00:23:33,333
- All right, time for my daily back rub.

565
00:23:33,333 --> 00:23:35,106
Who's going to do the honors?

566
00:23:35,106 --> 00:23:38,280
- Joel, none of us have working arms.

567
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:40,053
- I know.

568
00:23:40,053 --> 00:23:43,553
('60s action movie music)

569
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:51,866
- Hey Joel, what is that thing?

570
00:23:51,866 --> 00:23:54,760
- It's all part of my diabolical plan.

571
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:56,826
- But it's just a useless
prop that you built.

572
00:23:56,826 --> 00:23:58,746
It's not even connected to anything.

573
00:23:58,746 --> 00:23:59,733
- I know.

574
00:23:59,733 --> 00:24:02,480
('60s action movie music)

575
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,980
(kisses Crow)

576
00:24:13,189 --> 00:24:15,174
- Joel, is there any point to this?

577
00:24:15,174 --> 00:24:16,588
I've got a lot of work to do.

578
00:24:16,588 --> 00:24:19,668
Would you mind telling us
what this is all about?

579
00:24:19,668 --> 00:24:20,748
That's it.

580
00:24:20,748 --> 00:24:22,054
('60s action movie music)

581
00:24:22,054 --> 00:24:23,241
- I've had enough.

582
00:24:23,241 --> 00:24:24,374
- Joel, you're ruining it for me.

583
00:24:24,374 --> 00:24:26,041
- I know.

584
00:24:38,013 --> 00:24:39,400
- [Crow] Really funny sketch, Joel.

585
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:40,480
- [Joel] I know.

586
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:42,360
- [Voiceover] Wait until
the judge gives his verdict.

587
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:43,693
What else can you do?

588
00:24:43,693 --> 00:24:46,546
Don't forget we have a
corpse to deal with here.

589
00:24:46,546 --> 00:24:47,379
- [Tom] Corpse?

590
00:24:47,379 --> 00:24:48,746
- And Ms. Yachuko's disappeared, too.

591
00:24:48,746 --> 00:24:49,880
Sorry, doctor.

592
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,826
- [Joel] "I'm talking to Fudgy the Whale."

593
00:24:51,826 --> 00:24:52,960
- You are to remain at our disposal

594
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:55,335
until the investigation is over.

595
00:24:55,335 --> 00:24:57,320
- How long will that take?

596
00:24:57,320 --> 00:24:58,893
- We're moving as fast as we can,

597
00:24:58,893 --> 00:25:01,466
but please don't set foot
outside the limits of Monte Carlo

598
00:25:01,466 --> 00:25:03,480
until you get the okay from us.

599
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:05,480
- But I have to go back
to Columbia University.

600
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:08,440
I have some operations that are waiting.

601
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,973
I can't remain here indefinitely.

602
00:25:09,973 --> 00:25:13,473
- [Crow] "The former Ms. Moneypenny, sir."

603
00:25:14,402 --> 00:25:15,666
- Your Highness.

604
00:25:15,666 --> 00:25:16,973
- [Voiceover] There's your man, Commander.

605
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:20,320
- [Tom] "I hope you'll
be very happy together."

606
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:22,000
- [Joel] "Oh, he's hardly Sean, I realize,

607
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,833
"but he comes cheap."

608
00:25:25,146 --> 00:25:27,646
- [Crow] The Osterman Weekend.

609
00:25:28,653 --> 00:25:30,773
- Ms. Yachuko was right.

610
00:25:30,773 --> 00:25:31,733
- [Tom] "That's an ugly beard."

611
00:25:31,733 --> 00:25:32,920
- You can see the resemblance.

612
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:33,753
- [Joel] "To John Sexton."

613
00:25:33,753 --> 00:25:34,586
- Think so?

614
00:25:34,586 --> 00:25:36,466
I'm not so sure of that.

615
00:25:36,466 --> 00:25:39,746
Really, I don't think he's
quite so good looking.

616
00:25:39,746 --> 00:25:40,906
- [Crow] "Oh yeah?"

617
00:25:40,906 --> 00:25:42,640
- Why don't we shave the beard off,

618
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:43,666
just to make sure.

619
00:25:43,666 --> 00:25:44,499
- [Joel] Just peel it off.

620
00:25:44,499 --> 00:25:45,983
- The beard is mine, I'm attached to it.

621
00:25:45,983 --> 00:25:48,180
I want it to remain right there.

622
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:51,460
And furthermore, I'd like to
know what's going on here.

623
00:25:51,460 --> 00:25:52,340
- I'm Cunningham,

624
00:25:52,340 --> 00:25:55,233
of Allied Counter-Espionage
for Western Europe.

625
00:25:55,233 --> 00:25:56,393
- [Tom] "And I'm the Elephant King."

626
00:25:56,393 --> 00:25:58,233
- This is Ms. Maxwell, my assistant.

627
00:25:58,233 --> 00:26:00,807
You're the brother of our top agent.

628
00:26:00,807 --> 00:26:01,913
- [Crow] "Michael Ovitz."

629
00:26:01,913 --> 00:26:04,527
- So I think we can trust you.

630
00:26:04,527 --> 00:26:06,820
(Tom singing) ♫ Dominica Nica Nica ♫

631
00:26:06,820 --> 00:26:08,987
- [Joel] The flirting nun!

632
00:26:09,873 --> 00:26:14,040
- [Tom] "Still got it." (chuckles)

633
00:26:15,033 --> 00:26:16,687
- [Crow] Hm, Swiss steak for lunch.

634
00:26:16,687 --> 00:26:18,104
Lucky guy.

635
00:26:19,540 --> 00:26:20,673
- [Tom] "I'd like to make a confession.

636
00:26:20,673 --> 00:26:24,756
"I think you're hot." (chuckles)

637
00:26:27,021 --> 00:26:29,847
- [Joel] You know, Dave Barry's not funny.

638
00:26:29,847 --> 00:26:31,273
(sniffs)

639
00:26:31,273 --> 00:26:32,900
- [Crow] I should have used Mitchum.

640
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:35,983
- [Joel] Turn your head, you're fine.

641
00:26:38,292 --> 00:26:39,129
- Drop that knife.

642
00:26:39,129 --> 00:26:40,031
- [Tom] "Do you mind?

643
00:26:40,031 --> 00:26:42,636
"We're playing war games."

644
00:26:42,636 --> 00:26:45,495
- [Joel] What, does he have
a fur ball or something?

645
00:26:45,495 --> 00:26:47,822
- Drop it, I said.

646
00:26:47,822 --> 00:26:50,477
(grunting in pain)

647
00:26:50,477 --> 00:26:53,835
- [Crow] "I am the walrus,
goo goo g..." (exhales)

648
00:26:53,835 --> 00:26:55,782
- [Tom] Gee, I think I
had her in eighth grade.

649
00:26:55,782 --> 00:26:58,195
(devious music)

650
00:26:58,195 --> 00:26:59,635
- [Joel] "Now,

651
00:26:59,635 --> 00:27:01,552
time for his catheter."

652
00:27:03,022 --> 00:27:04,702
- [Crow] She's a flibbertigibbet.

653
00:27:04,702 --> 00:27:05,569
A will of the wisp.

654
00:27:05,569 --> 00:27:06,402
A clown.

655
00:27:06,402 --> 00:27:08,422
- [Tom] "I want this problem
called Maria taken care of,

656
00:27:08,422 --> 00:27:09,589
"permanently."

657
00:27:11,609 --> 00:27:13,942
- [Joel] Sister Mary Mayhem.

658
00:27:14,915 --> 00:27:15,902
- [Crow] "Father, forgive me,

659
00:27:15,902 --> 00:27:17,502
"for I have murdered."

660
00:27:17,502 --> 00:27:18,662
- [Tom] "Yea though I walk through shadow

661
00:27:18,662 --> 00:27:20,095
"of the valley of..."

662
00:27:20,095 --> 00:27:21,184
- [Joel] "Death."

663
00:27:21,184 --> 00:27:22,931
- [Tom] Oh.

664
00:27:22,931 --> 00:27:25,514
(weapon fires)

665
00:27:27,784 --> 00:27:29,931
- [Crow] "Make me happy, how'd I do?"

666
00:27:29,931 --> 00:27:31,848
- [Joel] "She is good."

667
00:27:33,259 --> 00:27:35,117
- [Tom] See? There is a role
for women in the church.

668
00:27:35,117 --> 00:27:38,117
Sisters are doing it for themselves.

669
00:27:39,411 --> 00:27:42,411
- [Crow] Sin and the art of archery.

670
00:27:43,544 --> 00:27:47,711
(Tom sings quietly) ♫ Mother
Superior jumped the gun ♫

671
00:27:48,894 --> 00:27:50,624
- [Crow] "This handy
hostage packs into a compact

672
00:27:50,624 --> 00:27:54,837
"nine by 14 case, hard
case also available."

673
00:27:54,837 --> 00:27:58,004
- [Joel] She's making a human burrito.

674
00:27:59,944 --> 00:28:01,276
(Tom Humming)

675
00:28:01,276 --> 00:28:02,109
- [Tom] Make it snappy, Sister,

676
00:28:02,109 --> 00:28:03,080
we've got other pick ups.

677
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:03,913
Come on!

678
00:28:05,324 --> 00:28:09,217
- [Joel] "I'm married
to the Lord, you know."

679
00:28:09,217 --> 00:28:13,217
Oh boy, I'd kill for a
jump cut right about now.

680
00:28:15,390 --> 00:28:16,552
- [Crow] "Oh Lord, please let my work

681
00:28:16,552 --> 00:28:18,379
"reflect thee in thine eyes."

682
00:28:18,379 --> 00:28:21,151
- [Tom] The few, the proud, the Opus Dei.

683
00:28:21,151 --> 00:28:25,151
(Tom singing jokingly in Latin)

684
00:28:28,179 --> 00:28:30,712
- [Joel] Is this a
documentary on how to do this,

685
00:28:30,712 --> 00:28:32,129
whatever this is?

686
00:28:34,272 --> 00:28:35,939
- [Crow] Oh, oh she's
a stunt nun, you know.

687
00:28:35,939 --> 00:28:40,225
I saw her get interviewed
on the Sci-Fi channel.

688
00:28:40,225 --> 00:28:42,154
- [Tom] Sheeze. Send
her to an outward bound,

689
00:28:42,154 --> 00:28:44,071
and this is the result.

690
00:28:45,629 --> 00:28:46,714
- [Joel] Now this is when you sit back

691
00:28:46,714 --> 00:28:49,297
and watch it all come together.

692
00:28:53,154 --> 00:28:57,541
(Crow singing) ♫ Let Hertz
put you in the ambulance ♫

693
00:28:57,541 --> 00:29:00,501
- [Tom] Looks like Turk 182.

694
00:29:00,501 --> 00:29:02,794
- [Joel] "We'll have her back tomorrow."

695
00:29:02,794 --> 00:29:03,627
- [Crow] "Human cleaners:

696
00:29:03,627 --> 00:29:06,627
"we'll clean your humans overnight."

697
00:29:09,145 --> 00:29:12,128
- [Tom] "Dodge vans:
more room, same ride."

698
00:29:12,128 --> 00:29:13,861
- [Joel] Now, let's review the steps

699
00:29:13,861 --> 00:29:16,994
on how to run a hostage down a rope."

700
00:29:16,994 --> 00:29:20,911
- [Crow] "Um, can we stop
at a Baskin Robbins?"

701
00:29:24,369 --> 00:29:27,194
- [Tom] Oh, they're repo clergy.

702
00:29:27,194 --> 00:29:28,501
- [Commander Cunningham] Dr. Connery,

703
00:29:28,501 --> 00:29:29,834
would you look at that photo?

704
00:29:29,834 --> 00:29:31,796
It was in Ms. Yachuko's bag.

705
00:29:31,796 --> 00:29:33,356
She said you know him.

706
00:29:33,356 --> 00:29:34,903
- It's Ward Jones.

707
00:29:34,903 --> 00:29:36,090
He was planning to marry her.

708
00:29:36,090 --> 00:29:36,996
- [Joel] "Then I showed up."

709
00:29:36,996 --> 00:29:38,823
- I met him when he took
my course in hypnosis.

710
00:29:38,823 --> 00:29:41,116
The one I gave in Japan.

711
00:29:41,116 --> 00:29:42,623
A very capable chap.

712
00:29:42,623 --> 00:29:43,730
- [Joel] "Thinks he's a chicken now."

713
00:29:43,730 --> 00:29:45,410
- I saw Jones killed this morning.

714
00:29:45,410 --> 00:29:46,770
- Ward's been killed?

715
00:29:46,770 --> 00:29:49,090
- By the same people that
tried to kidnap Yachuko.

716
00:29:49,090 --> 00:29:50,050
- [Tom] "The Shriners."

717
00:29:50,050 --> 00:29:51,556
- Thankfully, she's back in our hands.

718
00:29:51,556 --> 00:29:53,770
Ward had important information
he wanted to sell us.

719
00:29:53,770 --> 00:29:56,770
Unfortunately, he was killed
before he got it to us.

720
00:29:56,770 --> 00:29:59,023
- Actually, Ward asked
us to protect Yachuko

721
00:29:59,023 --> 00:30:01,410
because he'd given her
some secret information

722
00:30:01,410 --> 00:30:03,610
and he was afraid she might be in danger.

723
00:30:03,610 --> 00:30:05,578
Now, she denies this absolutely.

724
00:30:05,578 --> 00:30:06,799
- [Crow] Is this a Barnaby Jones wrap up?

725
00:30:06,799 --> 00:30:09,119
- And I'm inclined to think
she's telling the truth.

726
00:30:09,119 --> 00:30:11,625
- But we can't find any
explanation in this business.

727
00:30:11,625 --> 00:30:13,679
- Then I'll explain it to you.

728
00:30:13,679 --> 00:30:15,079
(Joel singing) ♫ What
happened was just this ♫

729
00:30:15,079 --> 00:30:16,812
- Ward had learned a
special yogi technique,

730
00:30:16,812 --> 00:30:19,172
quite complicated but very effective.

731
00:30:19,172 --> 00:30:21,252
Briefly, it's very
possible to communicate--

732
00:30:21,252 --> 00:30:22,799
- [Crow] "I'm not getting any of this."

733
00:30:22,799 --> 00:30:24,772
- in a state of hypnosis of total recall.

734
00:30:24,772 --> 00:30:26,945
The subject himself doesn't know he knows,

735
00:30:26,945 --> 00:30:28,652
but he would be able to repeat verbatim

736
00:30:28,652 --> 00:30:31,092
if he was again hypnotized
to the same extent.

737
00:30:31,092 --> 00:30:32,892
- Do you mean that's how Ward Jones--

738
00:30:32,892 --> 00:30:34,052
- Precisely.
- [Joel] "You're welcome."

739
00:30:34,052 --> 00:30:37,012
- It's clear Ward used Yachuko
as a human electronic brain,

740
00:30:37,012 --> 00:30:39,772
a sort of impregnable safe
to keep his secrets in.

741
00:30:39,772 --> 00:30:41,545
(imitating cuckoo clock)

742
00:30:41,545 --> 00:30:43,319
- A safe that you know
how to open, of course.

743
00:30:43,319 --> 00:30:45,092
- I'm sorry, but I can't help you.

744
00:30:45,092 --> 00:30:46,772
I'll be too busy for the next few days.

745
00:30:46,772 --> 00:30:47,839
- Why, Doctor?

746
00:30:47,839 --> 00:30:49,585
All you have to do is to
walk around Monte Carlo

747
00:30:49,585 --> 00:30:52,519
for the next few days until the
police decide to let you go.

748
00:30:52,519 --> 00:30:53,732
- [Tom] "Which I doubt."

749
00:30:53,732 --> 00:30:55,105
- And if I help you out,

750
00:30:55,105 --> 00:30:56,224
you'll get me out,

751
00:30:56,224 --> 00:30:57,625
is that what you mean?

752
00:30:57,625 --> 00:31:01,625
- Freedom always has a
price tag attached to it.

753
00:31:05,313 --> 00:31:08,146
- [Tom] "Oh, I guess we're early."

754
00:31:09,772 --> 00:31:10,784
(exhales)

755
00:31:10,784 --> 00:31:13,225
- [Joel] "I hate that suit."

756
00:31:13,225 --> 00:31:14,879
- Well, he's had it.

757
00:31:14,879 --> 00:31:16,919
- Poor guy.

758
00:31:16,919 --> 00:31:18,545
- I've never seen a
knife like that before.

759
00:31:18,545 --> 00:31:20,225
- [Tom] "One side's a
scaler and the other..."

760
00:31:20,225 --> 00:31:23,300
- Let's see if there are any clues.

761
00:31:23,300 --> 00:31:25,121
- [Crow] "He died listening to Rush."

762
00:31:25,121 --> 00:31:26,801
- [Tom] "2112."

763
00:31:26,801 --> 00:31:28,521
- Put it in the projector right away.

764
00:31:28,521 --> 00:31:30,147
He may have had time to get a photo.

765
00:31:30,147 --> 00:31:32,574
(chuckles)

766
00:31:32,574 --> 00:31:36,741
