1021
00:40:13,571 --> 00:40:15,598
- [Crow] "Let me get rearranged here."

1022
00:40:15,598 --> 00:40:18,425
- And to think this was
supposed to be my wedding night.

1023
00:40:18,425 --> 00:40:21,758
- I'm sorry to break up
your little tete-a-tete.

1024
00:40:21,758 --> 00:40:22,651
- [Joel] Tete.

1025
00:40:22,651 --> 00:40:24,051
- But we've received information

1026
00:40:24,051 --> 00:40:26,638
that Yachuko is being held
prisoner outside Granada.

1027
00:40:26,638 --> 00:40:29,131
- That's funny, the opposite direction.

1028
00:40:29,131 --> 00:40:30,811
- Who told you that?

1029
00:40:30,811 --> 00:40:31,745
- She told me.

1030
00:40:31,745 --> 00:40:33,798
(Tom singing) ♫ She told me ♫

1031
00:40:33,798 --> 00:40:35,745
- No, let her go,

1032
00:40:35,745 --> 00:40:38,078
or we might ruin everything.

1033
00:40:40,135 --> 00:40:41,642
- [Tom] Wow! What a cigarette.

1034
00:40:41,642 --> 00:40:43,495
(high pitched alarm sound)

1035
00:40:43,495 --> 00:40:45,002
(Yachuko crying out)

1036
00:40:45,002 --> 00:40:47,509
- [Crow] Maximum tanning.

1037
00:40:47,509 --> 00:40:50,176
- [Tom] The President's analyst.

1038
00:40:53,991 --> 00:40:55,375
- [Crow] You know, some
people can't wake up

1039
00:40:55,375 --> 00:40:58,292
no matter how many alarms they set.

1040
00:40:59,922 --> 00:41:01,029
- Stop now.

1041
00:41:01,029 --> 00:41:04,219
- [Tom] Looks like you
got an extra game there.

1042
00:41:04,219 --> 00:41:05,969
- [Joel] "Sacre bleu.

1043
00:41:07,737 --> 00:41:09,911
"Sacre bleu, huh?"

1044
00:41:09,911 --> 00:41:11,711
- [Crow] "Oh yeah, sacre bleu."

1045
00:41:11,711 --> 00:41:12,941
- [Tom] "Let's go lift now."

1046
00:41:12,941 --> 00:41:15,466
- [Joel] "You're looking good."

1047
00:41:15,466 --> 00:41:17,673
- It's all right, you can rest.

1048
00:41:17,673 --> 00:41:18,610
Calm down.

1049
00:41:18,610 --> 00:41:19,848
- [Tom] Martha Graham with her hair down.

1050
00:41:19,848 --> 00:41:22,608
- They've made you suffer, haven't they.

1051
00:41:22,608 --> 00:41:24,582
How can they make such a
pretty girl suffer like that?

1052
00:41:24,582 --> 00:41:26,702
- [Crow] "I'm asking
myself the same thing."

1053
00:41:26,702 --> 00:41:28,275
- You mustn't be afraid of me.

1054
00:41:28,275 --> 00:41:30,302
- [Joel] "Here, have
some new Miller Clear."

1055
00:41:30,302 --> 00:41:33,885
- We women understand
each other, don't we?

1056
00:41:36,399 --> 00:41:37,715
Here.

1057
00:41:37,715 --> 00:41:40,275
- [Tom] "Water. It's what's for dinner."

1058
00:41:40,275 --> 00:41:43,038
- Drink, it'll do you good.

1059
00:41:43,038 --> 00:41:44,595
- [Crow] "Your bread will be out shortly.

1060
00:41:44,595 --> 00:41:47,208
"I'll let you look at the menu."

1061
00:41:47,208 --> 00:41:48,715
- What do you want from me?

1062
00:41:48,715 --> 00:41:50,515
I told you I don't know anything.

1063
00:41:50,515 --> 00:41:53,048
I really don't know anything.

1064
00:41:53,048 --> 00:41:54,582
- Why are you so obstinate?

1065
00:41:54,582 --> 00:41:56,302
- [Joel] "I get it from my father."

1066
00:41:56,302 --> 00:41:58,942
- We know that Ward
confided something to you.

1067
00:41:58,942 --> 00:41:59,835
- It's not true.

1068
00:41:59,835 --> 00:42:01,808
No, it's not true.

1069
00:42:01,808 --> 00:42:03,142
It's not true.

1070
00:42:03,142 --> 00:42:04,888
How many times do I have to tell you

1071
00:42:04,888 --> 00:42:06,315
I don't know anything?

1072
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:07,148
- [Crow] "Four?"

1073
00:42:07,148 --> 00:42:09,417
- How can I convince you?

1074
00:42:09,417 --> 00:42:10,519
- If you talk,

1075
00:42:10,519 --> 00:42:14,071
I shall reward you in a
way you can't even imagine.

1076
00:42:14,071 --> 00:42:14,977
- [Tom] "I'll leave."

1077
00:42:14,977 --> 00:42:16,164
- You live with me.

1078
00:42:16,164 --> 00:42:17,207
- [Joel] "Do you smoke?"

1079
00:42:17,207 --> 00:42:18,396
- Like a princess.

1080
00:42:18,396 --> 00:42:20,663
- But I don't know anything.

1081
00:42:20,663 --> 00:42:22,046
I swear it. (screams)

1082
00:42:22,046 --> 00:42:24,713
- [Joel] Welcome to noogie hell.

1083
00:42:25,747 --> 00:42:26,580
- [Tom] "Hello, Vincent."

1084
00:42:26,580 --> 00:42:27,413
- [Crow] "Hello, Theo."

1085
00:42:27,413 --> 00:42:28,246
- [Tom] "Where is Vincent?"

1086
00:42:28,246 --> 00:42:30,272
- [Crow] "I'm here, Theo."

1087
00:42:30,272 --> 00:42:34,256
- [Tom] "Geese, I feel like
Gargan in frickin Tahiti, here."

1088
00:42:34,256 --> 00:42:35,242
- [Joel] "Man, I'm really hot.

1089
00:42:35,242 --> 00:42:36,075
"Are you hot?"

1090
00:42:36,075 --> 00:42:37,492
"Geese, I'm hot."

1091
00:42:41,062 --> 00:42:45,229
- [Crow] "Charlie, you're
my knight in shining armor."

1092
00:42:48,042 --> 00:42:50,309
- [Joel] "Hey Greg, heard
it through the grapevine."

1093
00:42:50,309 --> 00:42:52,629
(chuckles)

1094
00:42:52,629 --> 00:42:54,282
- Is that darn thing going to work?

1095
00:42:54,282 --> 00:42:56,722
- [Tom] Operation Double 00-Heehaw.

1096
00:42:56,722 --> 00:42:58,002
- If my calculations are correct,

1097
00:42:58,002 --> 00:42:59,776
the short circuit should
cause a return of current

1098
00:42:59,776 --> 00:43:03,669
capable of blowing up the
turret with the ammunition.

1099
00:43:03,669 --> 00:43:07,336
- [Joel] "Anyway, I got
Lulu backing me up."

1100
00:43:08,989 --> 00:43:11,656
- [Crow] "Hoody hoo! Hoody hoo!"

1101
00:43:16,091 --> 00:43:17,890
(small explosion)

1102
00:43:17,890 --> 00:43:19,216
- [Tom] "This is your
local utility company

1103
00:43:19,216 --> 00:43:20,526
"reminding you to call before you arch."

1104
00:43:20,526 --> 00:43:23,606
(explosion)

1105
00:43:23,606 --> 00:43:25,523
- [Joel] Fran Lebowitz!

1106
00:43:26,980 --> 00:43:27,873
Let's beat it.

1107
00:43:27,873 --> 00:43:30,206
- [Tom] Allons-y, everybody.

1108
00:43:37,420 --> 00:43:40,337
(MST3K theme song)

1109
00:43:43,686 --> 00:43:44,519
- Hi!

1110
00:43:44,519 --> 00:43:45,753
Welcome to a segment we like to call

1111
00:43:45,753 --> 00:43:48,660
"The Sean and Neil Show: Parallel Lives."

1112
00:43:48,660 --> 00:43:50,780
- In which we look at and contrast

1113
00:43:50,780 --> 00:43:53,820
the careers of Sean Connery
and his brother Neil Connery.

1114
00:43:53,820 --> 00:43:55,300
Star of today's movie.

1115
00:43:55,300 --> 00:43:58,206
- Yeah, this line represents Sean's life.

1116
00:43:58,206 --> 00:44:00,060
This one represents Neil's life.

1117
00:44:00,060 --> 00:44:01,220
Give you an example.

1118
00:44:01,220 --> 00:44:04,886
Sean's acting talent is
discovered at an early age

1119
00:44:04,886 --> 00:44:08,046
and leads to a long and
lucrative film career.

1120
00:44:08,046 --> 00:44:09,646
- While Neil's talent
for selling light bulbs

1121
00:44:09,646 --> 00:44:11,060
over the phone is discovered

1122
00:44:11,060 --> 00:44:14,060
leading to a long life of menial
jobs and aimless drifting.

1123
00:44:14,060 --> 00:44:18,050
- Well, up here is when Sean
gets his first million dollar

1124
00:44:18,050 --> 00:44:20,486
royalty check for the James Bond series.

1125
00:44:20,486 --> 00:44:23,646
- While Neil gets his first
$65 unemployment check

1126
00:44:23,646 --> 00:44:26,020
after being laid off
from The Cheese Factory.

1127
00:44:26,020 --> 00:44:26,853
- Yeah.

1128
00:44:26,853 --> 00:44:30,460
Here, Sean is declared Sexiest
Man Alive by People Magazine.

1129
00:44:30,460 --> 00:44:33,513
- While Neil is declared the
Stinky Cap Man in room 4B

1130
00:44:33,513 --> 00:44:36,153
by the other tenants in his SRO Hotel.

1131
00:44:36,153 --> 00:44:38,366
- Here, Sean calls the most powerful

1132
00:44:38,366 --> 00:44:39,980
and influential people in Hollywood

1133
00:44:39,980 --> 00:44:41,606
and is put through immediately.

1134
00:44:41,606 --> 00:44:43,206
- While Neil calls Pizza Hut

1135
00:44:43,206 --> 00:44:45,033
and is told that they won't deliver to him

1136
00:44:45,033 --> 00:44:46,406
because of bounced checks.

1137
00:44:46,406 --> 00:44:48,313
- Here, Sean is quoted as saying,

1138
00:44:48,313 --> 00:44:50,993
"During the making of 'The
Man Who Would Be King,'

1139
00:44:50,993 --> 00:44:54,006
"I had creative differences
with director John Huston."

1140
00:44:54,006 --> 00:44:55,633
- While Neil is quotes as saying,

1141
00:44:55,633 --> 00:44:57,460
"My manager at the Happy
Chef won't let me off

1142
00:44:57,460 --> 00:44:59,553
"for weekends, what a dink, man."

1143
00:44:59,553 --> 00:45:02,980
- Here, Sean goes to Spagos
and is seated immediately.

1144
00:45:02,980 --> 00:45:05,126
- While Neil's hotplate malfunction

1145
00:45:05,126 --> 00:45:07,316
and burns down his shabby furnished room."

1146
00:45:07,316 --> 00:45:09,102
- So Joel, what about
that point on the graph

1147
00:45:09,102 --> 00:45:11,455
where Sean's line actually
goes lower than Neil's?

1148
00:45:11,455 --> 00:45:13,348
- Oh, well that was the point

1149
00:45:13,348 --> 00:45:16,681
where Sean agreed to do
"Highlander 2: The Quickening,"

1150
00:45:16,681 --> 00:45:19,641
and ironically, that's when
Neil had to comfort Sean.

1151
00:45:19,641 --> 00:45:20,575
- Oh boy.

1152
00:45:20,575 --> 00:45:22,137
You know, we should remind
the nice folks out there

1153
00:45:22,137 --> 00:45:24,752
that this merely artistic
speculation on our part

1154
00:45:24,752 --> 00:45:26,299
of Neil Connery's life.

1155
00:45:26,299 --> 00:45:28,219
For all we know, he's
leading a prosperous,

1156
00:45:28,219 --> 00:45:30,192
happy existence on a farm in Scotland

1157
00:45:30,192 --> 00:45:32,126
with his beautiful wife
and adoring children.

1158
00:45:32,126 --> 00:45:33,379
- That's right, Tom.

1159
00:45:33,379 --> 00:45:35,699
And no matter what's
gone wrong with his life,

1160
00:45:35,699 --> 00:45:38,659
Neil can always look in the
mirror and say to himself,

1161
00:45:38,659 --> 00:45:40,632
"Well, at least I didn't do Zardoz."

1162
00:45:40,632 --> 00:45:42,232
- Right, and so Neil, wherever you are,

1163
00:45:42,232 --> 00:45:44,206
we would all just like to say...

1164
00:45:44,206 --> 00:45:45,339
(alarms ringing)

1165
00:45:45,339 --> 00:45:47,899
Oh, we've got movie time!

1166
00:45:47,899 --> 00:45:50,566
(doors opening)

1167
00:45:56,431 --> 00:45:58,005
- [Tom] That went well, don't
you think that went well?

1168
00:45:58,005 --> 00:45:58,838
- [Joel] Yes, it did.

1169
00:45:58,838 --> 00:45:59,688
- [Tom] Thought that went well.

1170
00:45:59,688 --> 00:46:00,521
- [Voiceover] Don't move.

1171
00:46:00,521 --> 00:46:02,229
- [Joel] "Okay, move."

1172
00:46:02,229 --> 00:46:03,736
- Let the girl go.

1173
00:46:03,736 --> 00:46:06,933
- [Crow] "If you love
your hostage, let her go."

1174
00:46:06,933 --> 00:46:08,433
- Drop that knife.

1175
00:46:10,694 --> 00:46:11,987
Drop it.

1176
00:46:11,987 --> 00:46:12,820
- [Tom] Junior Samples and Linda Hunt

1177
00:46:12,820 --> 00:46:15,831
in a deadly game of cat and mouse.

1178
00:46:15,831 --> 00:46:18,068
- Watch out.

1179
00:46:18,068 --> 00:46:19,223
(gun fire)

1180
00:46:19,223 --> 00:46:20,056
(cries out)

1181
00:46:20,056 --> 00:46:20,889
- [Joel] She's so calm.

1182
00:46:20,889 --> 00:46:23,227
Her roommate just got
shot and she's so calm.

1183
00:46:23,227 --> 00:46:24,075
- [Tom] The Sod Squad.

1184
00:46:24,075 --> 00:46:25,081
Julie, Pig, Eb.

1185
00:46:25,081 --> 00:46:25,998
- Let's go.

1186
00:46:30,131 --> 00:46:31,600
(gunfire)

1187
00:46:31,600 --> 00:46:33,634
- [Crow] (mumbles) are raining hot lead.

1188
00:46:33,634 --> 00:46:34,846
- Go on, I'll cover you.

1189
00:46:34,846 --> 00:46:37,686
(gunfire)

1190
00:46:37,686 --> 00:46:40,472
- [Joel] "Camlon coming through, Camlon!"

1191
00:46:40,472 --> 00:46:42,632
- [Tom] Katherine Hepburn is
the shakiest gun in the West.

1192
00:46:42,632 --> 00:46:44,882
(laughter)

1193
00:46:46,925 --> 00:46:49,258
- [Crow] "Cover me, Norman."

1194
00:46:52,369 --> 00:46:53,536
The Rocketeer!

1195
00:46:58,512 --> 00:47:01,762
Aw, it's the only way
he can talk to women.

1196
00:47:01,762 --> 00:47:02,896
- I am Ward.

1197
00:47:02,896 --> 00:47:04,522
- [Tom] "You are June."

1198
00:47:04,522 --> 00:47:08,202
- Ward. I told you
something about Thanatos.

1199
00:47:08,202 --> 00:47:10,416
Remember what I told you about Thanatos?

1200
00:47:10,416 --> 00:47:11,696
- Yes.

1201
00:47:11,696 --> 00:47:13,205
Thanatos.

1202
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:16,440
(Tom singing jokingly) ♫ Thanatos ♫

1203
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:18,488
- An atomic nucleus.

1204
00:47:18,488 --> 00:47:19,321
- Good.

1205
00:47:19,321 --> 00:47:20,901
What else did I tell you?

1206
00:47:20,901 --> 00:47:23,194
- Code 22.

1207
00:47:23,194 --> 00:47:24,901
Bar six.

1208
00:47:24,901 --> 00:47:26,421
Two words.

1209
00:47:26,421 --> 00:47:27,554
Tetouan.

1210
00:47:27,554 --> 00:47:29,981
- [Crow] "Two words. Bite. Me."

1211
00:47:29,981 --> 00:47:31,674
(mysterious music)

1212
00:47:31,674 --> 00:47:33,257
- [Tom] Judy Carne?

1213
00:47:35,794 --> 00:47:36,888
- [Joel] Wait a minute,

1214
00:47:36,888 --> 00:47:39,941
she looks like Sheil Zanyar now.

1215
00:47:39,941 --> 00:47:42,191
- [Crow] She's a Tony girl.

1216
00:47:46,968 --> 00:47:47,801
- Go on.

1217
00:47:47,801 --> 00:47:49,808
What happens in Tetouan?

1218
00:47:49,808 --> 00:47:50,994
- [Tom] "Watch Bond take shorthand."

1219
00:47:50,994 --> 00:47:53,381
- The blind work in Tetouan.

1220
00:47:53,381 --> 00:47:54,514
- [Joel] "Slow down."

1221
00:47:54,514 --> 00:47:56,168
- The blind die in Tetouan.

1222
00:47:56,168 --> 00:47:58,141
- [Joel] "In Tetouan. Just a second."

1223
00:47:58,141 --> 00:47:59,034
- The blind?

1224
00:47:59,034 --> 00:48:00,021
Try again.

1225
00:48:00,021 --> 00:48:01,248
(gunfire)

1226
00:48:01,248 --> 00:48:03,415
- [Crow] "Aw now come on."

1227
00:48:05,219 --> 00:48:09,386
- [Tom] Lady, you are due
back on the Space 1999 set.

1228
00:48:12,656 --> 00:48:17,394
- [Joel] Joan Jet just
walks in and she takes over.

1229
00:48:17,394 --> 00:48:18,354
- Sorry.

1230
00:48:18,354 --> 00:48:19,187
- [Crow] "It's nothing."

1231
00:48:19,187 --> 00:48:20,994
- I hoped to get here before she talked.

1232
00:48:20,994 --> 00:48:22,008
- [Tom] "Couldn't get a cab."

1233
00:48:22,008 --> 00:48:24,421
- Perhaps I could have saved you.

1234
00:48:24,421 --> 00:48:26,356
(gunfire)

1235
00:48:26,356 --> 00:48:30,078
- [Crow] "Oh, was I supposed to do that?"

1236
00:48:30,078 --> 00:48:30,911
- [Tom] "I'm-a pick it."

1237
00:48:30,911 --> 00:48:33,548
- [Crow] "And I'm-a kill it."

1238
00:48:33,548 --> 00:48:35,656
"Nice going, you just killed Sacagawea."

1239
00:48:35,656 --> 00:48:37,403
- What'd you get out of Yachuko?

1240
00:48:37,403 --> 00:48:39,616
- Nothing much, mostly in a sort of code.

1241
00:48:39,616 --> 00:48:41,005
It must be deciphered.

1242
00:48:41,005 --> 00:48:42,805
- [Tom] "As if I'm not busy enough."

1243
00:48:42,805 --> 00:48:45,458
- She spoke also of Tetouan.

1244
00:48:45,458 --> 00:48:48,005
Something strange, "The
blind they die in Tetouan."

1245
00:48:48,005 --> 00:48:49,805
- What else did she say to you?

1246
00:48:49,805 --> 00:48:51,431
- [Tom] "She wanted my
brother's autograph."

1247
00:48:51,431 --> 00:48:53,431
- It seems that Thanatos isn't joking.

1248
00:48:53,431 --> 00:48:55,498
They're planning to
steal an atomic nucleus.

1249
00:48:55,498 --> 00:48:57,058
- An atomic nucleus?

1250
00:48:57,058 --> 00:48:58,511
- [Joel] "Oh that's what
I used on the corn."

1251
00:48:58,511 --> 00:49:00,761
- Why, that's not possible.

1252
00:49:01,916 --> 00:49:05,952
- [Crow] "North Dakota,
before the apocalypse."

1253
00:49:05,952 --> 00:49:09,202
(Tom singing jokingly)

1254
00:49:14,005 --> 00:49:18,088
- [Crow] "Consider Northern
Illinois University."

1255
00:49:21,312 --> 00:49:23,979
- The atomic nucleus, and
only a Jeep for an escort.

1256
00:49:23,979 --> 00:49:27,779
- [Joel] Hey, "Here Come the
Brides" does a road show.

1257
00:49:27,779 --> 00:49:30,045
- [Crow] "Well, Matthew,
it's a herd of Miss Kitties."

1258
00:49:30,045 --> 00:49:33,514
- [Tom] They can hit 60 in brief spurts.

1259
00:49:33,514 --> 00:49:35,792
- [Joel] Tail hook takes it on the road.

1260
00:49:35,792 --> 00:49:36,875
- [Crow] Woo!

1261
00:49:38,579 --> 00:49:41,192
- [Tom] A few good men
meet a few naughty women.

1262
00:49:41,192 --> 00:49:42,912
(giggling)

1263
00:49:42,912 --> 00:49:43,745
Oh la la.

1264
00:49:44,739 --> 00:49:49,552
- [Crow] It's a man's life
in the new modern army.

1265
00:49:49,552 --> 00:49:52,952
- [Joel] "Our partridge
family van broke down."

1266
00:49:52,952 --> 00:49:55,869
- [Tom] She looks like an oil fire.

1267
00:49:57,584 --> 00:49:59,751
(mumbles)

1268
00:50:01,192 --> 00:50:05,037
